      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a good start for the emotion, but it feels a bit \"movie villain\" or overly dramatic. I want him to sound more grounded and actually convincing. Like, he shouldn't just be shouting about \"conscience\"—he needs to make a logical case for why the tech-led system is objectively failing. Can you rewrite it so he lays out a more specific, intellectual argument for why technocracy is a dead end for democracy?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
